# The daemon and exit demos run in WSL2; the vet gauntlet runs host-side.
# Everything checks out LF everywhere: host tests compare goldens byte-for-byte,
# and agent tooling writes LF — a CRLF working tree only produces churn warnings
# and latent byte-identity traps. No .bat/.cmd files exist to need CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.expected.json text eol=lf
*.golden.txt text eol=lf
*.golden text eol=lf
*.golden.json text eol=lf
